.TH LILI-CRASH 1 "September 2026" "lili-crash" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lili-crash \- find out why a program closed by itself
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lili-crash
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lili watches for programs that crash (systemd-coredump), a computer that froze, a Steam
game that closes right after starting, and an app that exits with an error as it opens.
She notifies each one and, with one click, opens an AI coding assistant (Claude Code,
Codex and others) in a terminal to find out why.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Programs that crashed, newest first, as JSON.
.TP
.BI mark " binary state" " \fR[\fIsummary\fR]"
Set a program to new, diagnosed, resolved or ignored.
.TP
.BI notify " id"
Show the notification for one crash (a PID), freeze (boot), Steam game (steam-...) or
app that didn't open (launch-...).
.TP
.B watch
Notify every new event; the lili-crash user service runs this.
.TP
.B open
Lili's window: AI usage and crash history.
.TP
.BI diagnose " id" " \fR...\fR"
Open the AI in a terminal to find out why.
.TP
.BR config " [\fBset\fR \fIkey value\fR]"
Settings shared with the tray widget.
.TP
.BI install " agent"
Run an AI assistant's official installer in a terminal.
.TP
.BR skill " \fBpath\fR|\fBview\fR|\fBedit\fR|\fBreset\fR"
This distribution's notes for the diagnosis skill.
.TP
.B setup
Per-user setup after installing a package: turns the service on, puts Lili in the
system tray and links the diagnosis skill for Claude and Codex.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lili/
Settings and your edited distribution notes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lili/
What you marked as diagnosed, resolved or ignored.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coredumpctl (1),
https://github.com/cryptoconspiracy/lili-crash
